  "notes": "The technical, double-time MC of the roster, and every parameter here exists to get out of the vocal's way. The research is unusually direct about it: harder and straighter 2&4 with fewer swing artifacts (`swing` 0.52 against the genre's 0.57, `quantizeStrength` 0.92), a kick that \"tightens toward two-per-bar\" (`densityPerBar` 2–3, syncopation cut to 0.22), hats \"mostly closed 16ths so the vocal density reads\" (open hats down to 0.08), sparse voicing leaving the mid-range clear (melody floor lifted to 76, counter `densityRatio` at the 0.32 minimum because the research says the countermelody is minimal *by design*). ⚠ **The bass is `mirror_kick`, and that is the research's reading rather than an engine limit**: \"sustained synth bass locked closer to the kick than classic g-funk — bass functions rhythmically, not melodically\". `followRootsProb` is 0.88 rather than 1.0 and the register spans 17 semitones so the line still has a reachable pool; `reese_sustain` is not used anywhere in this dataset. ⚠ `confidence` is `medium` and **the inferred block is `chords`** — the research marks the harmonic detail [LOW-CONF] and says it is deduced from his producer roster (Soopafly, Fredwreck, Battlecat) rather than from his records. The five families and the seventh-heavy extensions are that deduction; they are the first thing to revise if a better source appears. ⚠ The arrangement authors verses at 12–16 bars and a structure with no hook on two of its passes, because the research says album cuts have no chorus and posse cuts allocate 12–16 bars a voice.",
